3. Attribution and notices. Copies and redistributed modifications must retain the original copyright, attribution and license notices, identify “择命行效 · 常亮 / Zemingxingxiao · Chang Liang” in an appropriate attribution location, and include this license or a link to it. New contributions may have separate terms, but those terms must not remove recipients' existing rights to the original material under this license. Material modifications must be identified so that adaptations are not misrepresented as the author's original text. Reports created from the templates may carry concise attribution, the license name and a link in the footer instead of the full text.

4. Names, marks and theory. This license does not transfer trademarks, names or marks or permit impersonation or implied official endorsement. Necessary source attribution and reasonable citation remain permitted. Statements about authorship, copyright or registration describe original expression and provenance; they do not claim exclusive rights over general ideas, methods or public knowledge.

5. No warranty. Materials are provided as is, without guarantees of fitness, completeness or business outcomes to the extent permitted by law. Diagnoses support judgment and are not the sole basis for business or investment decisions. Users are responsible for their decisions, third-party rights and lawful use of supplied material. Liability that cannot legally be excluded is not excluded.

6. Interpretation. Both languages aim to express the same terms; the Chinese text governs interpretive differences. This is a project-specific free commercial use license, not a claim of MIT licensing or OSI certification.
